Source first (what actually calls out), resolver guard as defense in depth:
- Desktop auto-update (electron-builder publish / app-update.yml): generic feed from
  KLETRON_UPDATE_URL only; unset => publish null, no feed, never GitHub NousResearch.
- Desktop remote installer (bootstrap-runner): KLETRON_INSTALL_SOURCE only; unset => refused.
- `hermes update` / `kletron update`: channel pointers live on hermes-assets.nousresearch.com
  (source_releases._PUBLIC_BASE) => unresolvable, the update reports "unavailable".
- Automatic GitHub content fetches (model catalog fallback, local-runtime catalog refresh of
  NousResearch/hermes-agent@main) => hermes_cli/kletron_sources.py, empty by default.
- Resolver guard: Python stdlib resolver (hermes_cli/kletron_netguard.py, hooked in
  hermes_cli/__init__.py, imported by every entry point) and Electron (host-resolver-rules,
  Node dns, webRequest filter for github NousResearch paths). No HTTP client is patched.
- Telemetry: upstream defaults already off + consent-gated; asserted, not patched.

Owner: Romain Magnin (Kletron)
Test: tests/kletron/test_netguard.py; apps/desktop/electron/kletron-netguard.test.ts
Forwarded: not-needed (fork policy: nothing is asked of upstream)
Upstreamable: partial
Budget: see kletron/tools/budget.py (target <= 150 contact lines)
